  - mantis
  - mantises
  info: 'Mantodea, or mantises, are an order of insects distributed worldwide in
    temperate and tropical habitats. Mantises are identified by their triangular
    heads and large, bulging eyes. They have enlarged forelegs adapted for catching
    and gripping prey. Mantises are apex predators in the insect world that ambush
    their prey.


    Source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantis '
  image: {fileID: 2800000, guid: b5bca090a88b6ac45a5cab67f085a11a, type: 3}
